v 0.4.0 (in progress)
---------------------
* Added
    * Omega (e-e-e) three-electron backflow term: OMEGA TERM block reader/writer,
      analytical value/gradient/laplacian and their parameter derivatives,
      no-cusp and particle-symmetry constraints, and varmin/emin support
      (parameter mask, scale, constraint matrix, projector, parameter derivatives).
      Note that PyCasino constrains the K_lmn to be symmetric under index exchange,
      while CASINO up to at least v2.13.1313 imposes the opposite sign and so makes
      them antisymmetric; omega parameters are not interchangeable between the codes
      until that is resolved.
    * AGP/geminal wave function (``psi_s : geminal``): casino/geminal.py, GEMINAL block
      reader for parameters.casl, and the pfaffian design doc (Milestone 1); the
      Hartree-Fock default geminal reproduces the Slater determinant
    * slater.tressian_dot method returning third derivatives pre-contracted with the
      backflow Jacobian, and its documentation in slater.rst
    * Quick start guide and MPI parallelisation page in documentation
    * Documented all previously undocumented input keywords (GAUTOL, OPT_DTVMC, OPT_MAXITER,
      OPT_NOCTF_CYCLES, POSTFIT_VMC, OPT_FIXNL, VM_SMOOTH_LIMIT, VM_W_MAX, VM_W_MIN,
      EMIN_XI_VALUE, DMC_METHOD, LIMDMC, ALIMIT, NUCLEUS_GF_MODS, EBEST_AV_WINDOW, BACKFLOW)
    * drift_velocity and energy_parameters_d1 sections in wfn.rst
    * OPT_ORBITALS and USE_TMOVE keywords in config.rst
    * DMC tutorial page (dmc.rst): drift-diffusion, velocity limiting, branching,
      population control, T-move, load balancing
    * VMC tutorial page (vmc.rst): the time step derived from the kinetic-energy sum rule
      Var(ln(psi'^2/psi^2)) = 8/3 * dtvmc^2 * <T>, with the two averages (over the proposal
      at fixed R, and over the chain) kept apart, so that the classic ts*sqrt(<T>) = 0.826
      appears as what is obtained by interchanging them and the fitted correction as the
      Jensen gap of that interchange; the three kinetic-energy estimators KEI/TI/FISQ and
      where each of them enters; the Thomas-Fermi estimate of <T>; the range of validity;
      the EBES sqrt(N) law; acceptance_ratio and optimize_vmc_step
    * VMC_DECORR_PERIOD = 0 now selects the decorrelation period that maximizes efficiency
      instead of silently falling back to 3. The correlation time is measured on the production
      block itself, where thinning by the current period turns the autocorrelation rho into
      rho**period, so inverting that recovers the correlation time of the unthinned walk. A block
      of 1e6 configurations pins it down to better than +-0.5 even on Be, where a dedicated
      calibration run of the length CASINO uses leaves an uncertainty of +-20
    * Level-shift stabilization of the emin linear method: bisection over the shift, which only
      solves the eigenvalue problem, finds the largest step that still keeps every parameter
      variation within the trust radius, and the four
      shifts from there are compared by the correlated sampling estimate of energy + 3 * error
      over the very same configurations. That error accounts both for the effective sample size of
      the reweighting and for the serial correlation left after VMC_DECORR_PERIOD thinning, which
      reaches a factor of two on Be and N and would otherwise make the threshold system dependent.
      The no-step candidate always takes part in the comparison, so a cycle can never make the
      target function worse, and eigenvalues below EMIN_MIN_ENERGY are discarded as spurious.
      New keywords EMIN_MIN_ENERGY and EMIN_VAR_PREFACTOR
* Fixes
    * vmc_step_graph divided the acceptance ratio by the electron count unconditionally, so every
      CBCS graph it produced was scaled down by that factor
    * the EBES acceptance ratio was divided by the electron count, but a step is recorded as
      accepted when at least one electron moved, so the quantity was 1 - (1 - a)**N over N and
      could never exceed 1/N. For N = 7 it stayed within 0.8% of 1/N while the true acceptance
      swept 50% to 90%, leaving the step-size fit blind and unable to reach its 50% target.
      The per-electron probability is now recovered by inverting that expression, and the whole
      measurement lives in one place, Casino.acceptance_ratio, shared with vmc_step_graph
    * correlation.data writer emitted a single eta cut-off line whatever the spin-dependence,
      and lost the "2=YES BUT NO SPIN-DEP" flag because it is stored as a boolean, so the
      written file could not be read back
    * PSI_S header printed a hardcoded ``slater`` regardless of the actual psi_s value
    * Input keywords parsed with wrong type: VM_W_MAX, VM_W_MIN, EMIN_XI_VALUE read as
      booleans instead of floats, NON_LOCAL_GRID as boolean instead of integer;
      LIMDMC misspelled as "limdmct" so the keyword was silently ignored
    * Misleading NUMBA_NUM_THREADS advice in parallel.rst: JIT kernels are single-threaded
    * Cusp initialisation description in cusp.rst: Cusp is created by CuspFactory,
      not by Slater
    * Missing underscores in DMC_EQUIL_NBLOCK and DMC_STATS_NBLOCK keyword names in config.rst
    * Third derivatives of Slater orbitals: yyy and zzz components of tressian_matrix
      used the x-component of the angular gradient, and tressian doubled one ordering
      of the triple-product trace instead of summing both (verified against numerical
      derivatives on Ne)
    * False trace-reversal identity in tressian snippets of slater.rst
    * Broken Numba documentation link in index.rst
    * Incorrect output description for kinetic_energy_parameters_d1 in wfn.rst
    * Missing backflow-parameters formula in kinetic_energy_parameters_d1 section of wfn.rst
    * Incorrect output description for nonlocal_energy_parameters_d1 and missing sign
      in kinetic energy derivative in wfn.rst
    * Methods summary in wfn.rst attributed to Slater class instead of Wfn
    * Duplicate Sphinx anchor ``intermediate data`` between jastrow.rst and backflow.rst
    * Duplicate Sphinx anchor ``value`` between wfn.rst and slater.rst
    * Typo "Input parameter are supported" → "Input parameters supported" in config.rst
    * emin linear method took Q = 1 / eigvector[0]**2 - 1, which holds only for an eigvector
      normalized in the S metric, while scipy.linalg.eig returns a Euclidean-normalized one,
      so the semi-orthogonalization rescaling of Δp was wrong whenever the derivatives were
      strongly correlated; Q is now evaluated as Δp · S · Δp
    * emin linear method divided by the standard deviation of every wave function derivative,
      so a parameter the sample does not depend on produced an infinite scale and a singular
      overlap matrix; such parameters are now excluded from the eigenproblem and left unchanged
* Improved
    * CBCS initial time step is now sqrt(3) * erfinv(1/2) * (1 + 0.045/nuclei) / sqrt(<T>) instead
      of one over the electron count, with <T> summed over the nuclei from the Thomas-Fermi
      expansion 0.7687*Z^(7/3) - 0.5*Z^2 + 0.2699*Z^(5/3) and
      nuclei = sum(Z^(7/3))^2 / sum(Z^(14/3)). Only the last constant is fitted. A uniform
      displacement by ts gives Var(ln(psi'^2/psi^2)) = 8/3 * ts^2 * <T> while detailed balance
      pins the mean of that log ratio to minus half its variance, so a gaussian one is accepted
      with probability 2*Phi(-sigma/2) and the 50% point sits at ts*sqrt(<T>) = sqrt(3)*erfinv(1/2)
      = 0.826; <T> = abs(E) follows from the virial theorem, and the Thomas-Fermi expansion reproduces
      the Hartree-Fock energies to 1.8% with no free constant. The remaining correction is the
      non-gaussianity of the log ratio, which falls off with the number of nuclei sharing <T>,
      since the drift is of order Z at a nucleus and outer shells contribute almost nothing
      to the tails.
      Measured on the seventeen systems in examples/time_step/CBCS the 50% acceptance point lands
      within 0.9% rms of the initial guess for atoms, ions, hydrides and hydrocarbons alike, where
      the old guess spread it over 0.61 to 1.86 and left molecules against the edge of the scanned
      range. The electron count deliberately does not appear: it equals sum(Z) only for a neutral
      system, and substituting it costs 27% on Be(2+)
    * Speed up backflow optimization: kinetic_energy_parameters_d1 uses slater.tressian_dot
      to avoid materializing the (3N)³ tressian tensor, vectorized bf_d1 loop and
      fused reduction loop in backflow_laplacian_parameters_d1
    * Cusp correction page expanded with physical motivation, correction scheme, and API reference

v 0.3.0 (2025-10-30)
--------------------
* Added
    * Documentation on https://casinoqmc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/
* Improved
    * Improve Jastrow speed by 20%
    * scipy.optimize.least_squares optimization in one thread
    * Add tests
* Fixes
    * Remove ``np.float_`` as it not supported in Numpy 2.X
    * Fix reweighted VMC variance optimization.

v 0.2.0 (2024-10-30)
--------------------
* Added
    * Pseudopotential for VMC and DMC (with T-move)
* Improved
    * Use Horner Scheme in Jastrow term
    * Electron-by-Electron (EBES) sampling in DMC
    * Use structrefs instead of jitclasses
* Fixes
    * System with only up- or only down- electrons (i.e H-atom)

v 0.1.0 (2023-10-30)
--------------------
* Added
    * Orbital file formats: gwfn.data, stowfn.data
    * Multi-determinant expansions
    * 3-term Jastrow factor and 3-term backflow transformation
    * Configuration-by-configuration (CBCS) sampling
    * Partial cusp correction according to A. Ma, M. D. Towler, N. D. Drummond, and R. J. Needs, without rc optimization
    * MPI parallelization
    * VMC and DMC energy calculation, varmin and emin optimization
